From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:19:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: ilp32: do not build the generic compat ELF loader on
 arm64

The ILP32 series builds the arm64 compat ELF loaders in the architecture
code: binfmt_elf32.c (AArch32, AARCH32_EL0) and binfmt_ilp32.c (ILP32)
both include fs/compat_binfmt_elf.c with their own definitions. In
5.10, COMPAT_BINFMT_ELF had to be selected by the architecture, and the
series dropped that select. Since then COMPAT_BINFMT_ELF became
"def_bool y" with "depends on COMPAT && BINFMT_ELF", so arm64 builds
fs/compat_binfmt_elf.o as well:

- with AARCH32_EL0=y, a second AArch32 ELF loader is registered
  (vmlinux has the initcalls of binfmt_elf32, binfmt_ilp32 and
  compat_binfmt_elf);
- with ARM64_ILP32=y and AARCH32_EL0=n, it does not build, as the
  compat ELF definitions belong to AArch32:
  include/linux/elfcore-compat.h: error: unknown type name 'compat_elf_gregset_t'

Do not enable COMPAT_BINFMT_ELF on arm64.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8e26aab8c1fcf3faaf208509b86840642362a09c)
(cherry picked from commit 8ecfdc020cab1b375df4ab2335002a719930c090)
---
 fs/Kconfig.binfmt | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/fs/Kconfig.binfmt
+++ b/fs/Kconfig.binfmt
@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@ config BINFMT_ELF_KUNIT_TEST
 config COMPAT_BINFMT_ELF
 	def_bool y
 	depends on COMPAT && BINFMT_ELF
+	# arm64 builds its AArch32 and ILP32 ELF loaders from compat_binfmt_elf.c
+	# itself (arch/arm64/kernel/binfmt_elf32.c, binfmt_ilp32.c)
+	depends on !ARM64
 	select ELFCORE
 
 config ARCH_BINFMT_ELF_STATE
